    "title": "Dricus du Plessis Retains UFC Middleweight Title in Sydney",
    "text": "• Dricus du Plessis retained his UFC middleweight title on February 9, 2025, in Sydney.\n• Du Plessis defeated Sean Strickland in a unanimous decision after a bloody fight.\n• The judges scored the fight 50-45, 50-45, and 49-46 in favor of Du Plessis.\n• Du Plessis broke Strickland's nose in the fourth round.\n• Strickland's face was bloodied throughout the fight, and he admitted to his team that he had re-injured his nose.\n• Du Plessis effectively used his left kick in the first two rounds.\n• Strickland attempted to mount a comeback in the third round but was outstruck overall.\n• In the main event, Zhang Weili retained her strawweight title against Tatiana Suárez by unanimous decision.\n• The event took place at Qudos Bank Arena in Sydney.\n• Quillan Salkilld Liviano made a successful UFC debut, finishing Anshul Juvo in 19 seconds.\n• Jake Matthews won his fight against Francisco Prado by unanimous decision.\n• Jimmy Crute fought to a majority draw against Rodolfo Bellato.\n• Tom Nolan lost to Viacheslav Borshchev by unanimous decision.\n• Colby Grosnesse lost his UFC debut to Aleksandre Topuria.\n• Jonathan Micallef lost to Kevin Jousset by points decision.\n• Jack Jenkins was stopped in the third round by Gabriel Santos.\n• Justin Tafa's fight against Tallison Teixeira was stopped in 35 seconds due to a referee's intervention.",
